				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				670,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): update workspace folder access from async to sync API\n\nUpdate WindServiceHandlers and CocoonService to use the new synchronous workspace folder API:\n- Replace `GetFolders().await` with `GetWorkspaceFolders()` in handlers for getFolders, findInFiles, and findFiles\n- Refactor addFolder and removeFolder to use direct folder manipulation via GetWorkspaceFolders/SetWorkspaceFolders instead of async AddFolder/RemoveFolder methods\n- Update getName handler to extract display name from first workspace folder synchronously\n- Fix field access: change `Folder.Uri` to `Folder.URI.to_string()` for consistency with the new DTO structure\n- Add missing `IgnoreFocusOut` field to the showInputBox handler\n\nThese changes align with the updated Common library API where workspace folder operations are now synchronous, removing the need for async/await in workspace folder handlers.",
			"SHA": "8b7e172c8e096c67392eafc196361e7cc8c7123f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T03:03:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				670,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): fix type mismatches and API changes in WindServiceHandlers\n\nCorrect several IPC handler implementations to match the updated Common library API contracts:\n\n- Storage: Replace non-existent `DeleteItem` with `UpdateStorageValue(true, Key, None)`, and fix `GetKeys` to use `GetAllStorage(true)` extracting keys from the returned object\n- QuickInput: Fix field names (`Placeholder` -> `PlaceHolder`), wrap optional bools in `Some()`, add `..Default::default()` for missing fields, and pass options wrapped in `Some()`\n- Workspaces: Update all handlers to use `ApplicationState.Workspace` instead of `Environment.Workspace`\n- Themes: Add required `ConfigurationOverridesDTO` parameter to `GetConfigurationValue` and `UpdateConfigurationValue`, fix null handling with proper `as_str()` call\n- Search: Update workspace access to use `ApplicationState.Workspace`\n\nThese changes resolve compilation errors and runtime failures caused by API drift between the handler implementations and the Common trait definitions.",
			"SHA": "241b13223edbd244f02fc228545eb3030e4ec46e"
		}
	],
